00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:13,419
we're saying that there's no negative ages here.

257
00:15:13,419 --> 00:15:16,659
We're saying that age is from when you're born and on.

258
00:15:16,659 --> 00:15:19,940
So one property that should hold for all inputs is

259
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:23,220
that the age never is never less than zero.

260
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:26,920
Boom, that is a property we could put in it

261
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:30,620
as a claim that we can make or proposition

262
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:32,299
that should hold for all inputs.

263
00:15:32,299 --> 00:15:36,079
Now with this random generator, we can generate

264
00:15:36,079 --> 00:15:39,859
millions and billions of inputs really cheaply.

265
00:15:39,859 --> 00:15:42,079
Now we're still just creating evidence.

266
00:15:42,079 --> 00:15:44,509
We still do not have a proof, but now

267
00:15:44,509 --> 00:15:46,939
look, we have like this random distribution and

268
00:15:46,939 --> 00:15:48,740
we can generate way more evidence.

269
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:54,259
So we can start to emulate a mathematical proof.

270
00:15:54,259 --> 00:15:57,009
We can emulate trying to get as close as

271
00:15:57,009 --> 00:15:59,759
possible to proof that all inputs are always going

272
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:00,919
to be correct.

273
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:01,919
But it's asymptotic.

274
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:02,919
We'll never actually get there.

275
00:16:02,919 --> 00:16:04,599
We will never get there.

276
00:16:04,599 --> 00:16:09,599
And there's still not enough computational resources to execute this thing for that long.

277
00:16:09,599 --> 00:16:11,639
Okay, so then what's next?

278
00:16:11,639 --> 00:16:13,159
What is the next step?

279
00:16:13,159 --> 00:16:14,719
And you could think of other properties.

