00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:43,879
that for a certain function, it behaves

290
00:16:43,879 --> 00:16:46,879
correctly under all inputs.

291
00:16:46,879 --> 00:16:51,000
Sorry, that behaves correctly.

292
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:57,799
What I'm actually saying is that certain properties hold for all inputs.

293
00:16:57,799 --> 00:17:02,679
And that is called formal verification.

