00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:28,759
verify software that would just be outrageously difficult to formally verify before.

300
00:17:28,759 --> 00:17:30,959
And so, sorry, I was trying to define formal verification still.

301
00:17:30,959 --> 00:17:39,159
So formal verification basically allows you to provide the mathematical proof that certain

302
00:17:39,159 --> 00:17:42,279
properties do hold under all inputs.

303
00:17:42,279 --> 00:17:45,420
And with enough cognitive effort, hopefully you can

304
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:48,559
come up with a set of properties or

305
00:17:48,559 --> 00:17:57,639
a set of propositions that are individually necessary and collectively sufficient to characterize

306
00:17:57,639 --> 00:18:02,119
the intended behavior of your functionality.

307
00:18:02,119 --> 00:18:07,359
I think that is the core thing to understand.

308
00:18:07,359 --> 00:18:11,079
And I mean, this would be absolutely just amazing

309
00:18:11,079 --> 00:18:14,799
if all of our software, not just crazy

310
00:18:14,799 --> 00:18:23,159
mathematical calculations, not just cryptographic primitives, not just like TCP, not low-level

